//? Title: Native vsim port: grasp skill and scheduler
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

> Native articulated robot physics: what limits the fruit sorter

This report runs the fruit-sorting workcell on datamunge's in-house rigid-body
engine (vsim, 960 Hz) with bounded effort servos and actual wrist RGB
classification. MuJoCo is absent from the standard build. An earlier version of
this page transferred the MuJoCo-trained dueling DQN scheduler unchanged and
showed a 20-second clip with zero sorts. Here we ask why, test two remedies (a
learned scheduler trained natively for longer, and a corrected grasp skill), and
keep whichever wins on held-out streams. Finally, we retrain the wrist-camera
classifier on native views, which removes wrong-bin sorts in closed-loop tests.

## Where the time goes

The scheduler only chooses *which* fruit to intercept and *when* (wait, early or
late on the leading fruit, early or late on the next one). The reach, close,
lift and drop motions are fixed inverse-kinematics skills. Instrumenting
10 simulated minutes of native runs at 0.4 fruit/s showed:

| Stage | Rate |
|---|---:|
| Arrivals that the arm attempts | about 50% |
| Attempts that end in a stable grasp | about 50% |
| Grasps that are sorted into the correct bin | about 85% |

A successful pick occupies the arm for about 7.6 s and a failed one for about
4.6 s, so the arm tops out near 4 sorts per minute: 0.4 fruit/s is roughly three
times its capacity, and most fruit must be missed whatever the scheduler does.

Can a better scheduler pick the fruit it will grasp? We logged 726 attempts with
the 25 observation features the scheduler sees and fitted logistic regression,
gradient boosting and a small neural network to predict grasp success. The
cross-validated AUC was only about 0.59 for all three. A neural reward or
success model therefore has little signal to exploit: grasp outcome is decided
mostly by contact details during closing, not by anything visible at decision
time.

## Grasp skill: two opt-in corrections

Tracing failed grasps in the intercept loop exposed two mechanical causes:

- The tool follows the moving fruit with a steady 13-15 mm lag, just above the
  fixed 12 mm alignment threshold, so the jaws often never start closing.
- The IK target is refitted every 8 physics ticks during closing. Once a finger
  touches, each refit jerks the forming grip; many failures held support for
  exactly 7 of the 24 required ticks.

`FruitStreamOptions` now exposes both as opt-in settings (defaults unchanged, so
other reports are unaffected): `grasp_alignment_tolerance` (0.005-0.05 m,
default 0.012) and `hold_grasp_target`, which stops re-aiming once the finger
reports contact. A sweep over 10 streams of 120 s showed that a 20 mm tolerance
with the target held raised correct sorts from 88 to 106 (grasp rate 0.49 to
0.59); wider tolerances gave no further gain. A larger lead or a refit on
every tick made results worse.

## Native scheduler training

With the corrected skill we trained schedulers natively for 96 windows of about
120 s each (3.3 simulated hours per run): DQN, double DQN (two seeds), dueling
double DQN and PPO, under the default reward and under a reshaped reward with
higher miss and wrong-bin costs and a queue-waiting cost. Arrival rates were drawn
from 0.1-0.45 fruit/s. The program below is kept for reproducibility but is not
run when this page is rebuilt (`eval="no"`). Run it with
`train 0 A 96 7 build/fruit_native_train` and similar for the other methods.

```{cpp, eval="no"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
namespace s = dm::sim;
namespace r = dm::rl;
// usage: train METHOD(0 DQN,1 DDQN,2 dueling DDQN,3 PPO) REWARD(A|B) WINDOWS SEED OUTDIR
int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  if (argc != 6)
    return 2;
  const int         method  = std::atoi(argv[1]);
  const std::string reward  = argv[2], out = argv[5];
  const std::size_t windows = std::stoul(argv[3]);
  const std::uint64_t seed  = std::stoull(argv[4]);
  std::filesystem::create_directories(out);
  const auto assets = dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm", "../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
  const auto urdf =
      (std::filesystem::path(assets) / "Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string();
  s::FruitStreamOptions o;
  o.articulated_physics = true;
  o.physics_backend     = s::ArticulatedBackend::Native;
  o.physics_timestep    = 1. / 960;
  o.active_capacity     = 8;
  o.watch_infeed = o.synchronized_grasp = true;
  o.training_error              = {.02, .02}; // synthetic labels isolate control
  o.grasp_alignment_tolerance   = .02;
  o.hold_grasp_target           = true;
  if (reward == "B") {
    o.queued_wait_cost = .5;
    o.miss_cost        = 6;
    o.wrong_cost       = 8;
  }
  s::FruitStreamEnvironment  env(urdf, o);
  r::DiscreteTrainingOptions fit;
  fit.model.method = r::DiscreteMethod(method);
  fit.model.seed = fit.seed = seed;
  fit.model.hidden          = 64;
  fit.windows               = windows;
  fit.learning_rate         = method == 3 ? .0003 : .0005;
  fit.warmup                = 256;
  fit.train_every           = 2;
  fit.target_every          = 256;
  fit.rollout               = 128;
  fit.epochs                = 8;
  fit.epsilon_start         = .3;
  fit.epsilon_end           = .03;
  std::ofstream log(out + "/training.csv");
  log << "window,seconds,reward,decisions,steps,updates,loss\n";
  fit.progress = [&](std::size_t k, const r::DiscreteWindow& w, const r::DiscretePolicy& p) {
    log << std::format("{},{:.3f},{:.4f},{},{},{},{:.6f}\n", k, w.seconds, w.reward,
                       w.decisions, w.environment_steps, w.updates, w.loss);
    log.flush();
    if ((k + 1) % 16 == 0)
      p.save(out + std::format("/ckpt_{}.npz", k + 1));
  };
  auto result = r::train_discrete(s::stream_learning_environment(env, .1, .45), fit);
  result.policy.save(out + "/final.npz");
  std::cout << "done " << out << '\n';
}
```

Every checkpoint (every 16 windows, 36 in all) was scored on six validation
streams of 90 s at 0.4 fruit/s, separate from the test streams used below.
Training rewards stayed flat, and no checkpoint beat the simple greedy rule
(intercept whenever any option is feasible, preferring the leading fruit late):

| Scheduler (validation, 6 x 90 s) | Attempts | Grasped | Correct |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Greedy rule | 86 | 55 | 44 |
| Best native DQN (window 96) | 61 | 40 | 34 |
| Best double DQN (window 80) | 49 | 35 | 32 |
| Best PPO (window 16) | 61 | 37 | 31 |
| Reshaped-reward runs, best | 62 | 33 | 29 |

The learned schedulers wait more often than the greedy rule. Given the AUC
result, waiting buys little: an attempt that is never made can never succeed.
The best native checkpoint and its
[training log|file:figures/fruit_native_port_dqn_training.csv] are kept in
`figures/` and enter the test comparison.

## Held-out comparison

Eight test streams of 90 s at 0.4 fruit/s (seeds not used for training or
selection), with synthetic 98%-accurate labels so that only control differs.
Each stream runs in its own environment on its own thread.

```{cpp, results="markdown", nix-shell="git+file:../../..#cpp", cmd="export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=$(printenv DATAMUNGE_CAD_PKG_CONFIG_PATH || printenv PKG_CONFIG_PATH); c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && DATAMUNGE_LINKED_CORE=$(pkg-config --variable=prefix datamunge) OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 {bin}"}
#include <algorithm>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <future>
#include <iostream>
#include <print>
#include <thread>
namespace s = dm::sim;
namespace r = dm::rl;
// One scheduler on one skill configuration, scored on held-out native streams.
struct Candidate {
  std::string name, policy; // policy: checkpoint path, or empty for the greedy rule
  bool        improved_skill;
};
struct Score {
  std::uint64_t arrivals{0}, attempts{0}, grasped{0}, correct{0}, wrong{0}, missed{0};
};
s::FruitStreamOptions workcell(bool improved_skill) {
  s::FruitStreamOptions o;
  o.articulated_physics = true;
  o.physics_backend     = s::ArticulatedBackend::Native;
  o.physics_timestep    = 1. / 960;
  o.active_capacity     = 8;
  o.watch_infeed = o.synchronized_grasp = true;
  o.training_error                      = {.02, .02}; // synthetic labels: isolates control
  if (improved_skill) {
    o.grasp_alignment_tolerance = .02;
    o.hold_grasp_target         = true;
  }
  return o;
}
// Greedy rule: intercept whenever any option is feasible, preferring the leader late.
std::size_t greedy(const r::DiscreteObservation& x) {
  for (std::size_t a : {2, 1, 4, 3})
    if (x.allowed[a])
      return a;
  return 0;
}
Score run(const std::string& urdf, const Candidate& c, std::uint64_t seed, double seconds) {
  s::FruitStreamEnvironment env(urdf, workcell(c.improved_skill));
  std::optional<r::DiscretePolicy> policy;
  if (!c.policy.empty())
    policy = r::DiscretePolicy::load(c.policy);
  auto frame = env.reset(seed, .4);
  while (frame.time < seconds) {
    auto x = env.learning_observation();
    frame  = env.step(s::StreamAction(policy ? policy->action(x) : greedy(x))).frame;
  }
  const auto& n = frame.counts;
  return {n.arrivals, n.attempts, n.grasped, n.correct, n.wrong, n.missed};
}
int main() {
  const auto assets = dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm", "../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
  const auto urdf =
      (std::filesystem::path(assets) / "Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string();
  const std::vector<Candidate> candidates{
      {"MuJoCo-trained DQN", "figures/fruit_stream_physics_rl/dueling_dqn_256.npz", false},
      {"Greedy rule", "", false},
      {"Greedy rule", "", true},
      {"MuJoCo-trained DQN", "figures/fruit_stream_physics_rl/dueling_dqn_256.npz", true},
      {"Native-trained DQN", "figures/fruit_native_port_dqn.npz", true}};
  const int    streams = 8;
  const double seconds = 90;
  // Independent environments are single-writer; run each stream on its own thread.
  std::vector<std::future<Score>> jobs;
  for (const auto& c : candidates)
    for (int k = 0; k < streams; ++k)
      jobs.push_back(std::async(std::launch::async, run, urdf, c, 2026110300 + k, seconds));
  std::println("| Scheduler | Grasp skill | Arrivals | Attempts | Grasped | Correct | Wrong | Missed |");
  std::println("|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < candidates.size(); ++i) {
    Score t;
    for (int k = 0; k < streams; ++k) {
      auto x = jobs[i * streams + k].get();
      t.arrivals += x.arrivals, t.attempts += x.attempts, t.grasped += x.grasped;
      t.correct += x.correct, t.wrong += x.wrong, t.missed += x.missed;
    }
    std::println("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |", candidates[i].name,
                 candidates[i].improved_skill ? "aligned 20 mm + hold" : "original", t.arrivals,
                 t.attempts, t.grasped, t.correct, t.wrong, t.missed);
  }
}
```

// result_begin: markdown
| Scheduler | Grasp skill | Arrivals | Attempts | Grasped | Correct | Wrong | Missed |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| MuJoCo-trained DQN | original | 298 | 123 | 51 | 42 | 0 | 239 |
| Greedy rule | original | 300 | 125 | 55 | 49 | 0 | 230 |
| Greedy rule | aligned 20 mm + hold | 302 | 118 | 75 | 68 | 0 | 213 |
| MuJoCo-trained DQN | aligned 20 mm + hold | 296 | 119 | 54 | 50 | 0 | 230 |
| Native-trained DQN | aligned 20 mm + hold | 300 | 71 | 45 | 40 | 0 | 240 |
// result_end

## Wrist classifier for the native camera

The comparison above uses synthetic labels. The deployed system instead
classifies each fruit from one wrist-camera crop taken just before the arm
descends, and that single label chooses the bin. The MobileNet used so far was
adapted to 256 px crops from MuJoCo runs (256 training crops, all at the
inspection moment). The native port uses a 128 px camera, so its inputs never
matched that training data. On held-out native streams the old model labelled
only 72% of inspection crops correctly; apples were close to chance. In the
video, where the model is rerun on every frame through the grasp, lift and drop,
its label flipped between consecutive frames 27% of the time.

We therefore collected training data from the deployed setup: 224 native streams
of 120 s at 0.4 fruit/s, run by the greedy scheduler with the corrected grasp.
Each crop comes from the 128 px camera, labelled by the true fruit class. The
data hold the 4,188 inspection crops plus 4 fps views of the current target (or
next belt fruit) through approach, grasp, lift and release, 70,186 crops in all.
Streams are split by seed: 80% train, 10% validation (selects the epoch), 10%
test. A MobileNet twice as wide as before (width 0.25) was trained from scratch
on every training crop and its mirror image, with inspection crops weighted
three times. The program below collects the data in 28 worker processes (about 2 h on
32 cores), trains for 25 epochs (under an hour; validation selects epoch 16) and
writes `figures/fruit_native_port_mobile.npz`. Like the scheduler training, it
is not run when this page is rebuilt (`eval="no"`). Run it from this directory
with `vision 28 8 120 25 build/fruit_native_vision`.

```{cpp, eval="no"}
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <unistd.h>
namespace s = dm::sim;
namespace n = dm::nn;
// usage: vision WORKERS STREAMS SECONDS EPOCHS OUTDIR
// Workers 0..80% train, next 10% validation, last 10% test (split by stream seed).
constexpr int P = 64 * 64 * 3;
std::size_t greedy(const dm::rl::DiscreteObservation& x) {
  for (std::size_t a : {2, 1, 4, 3})
    if (x.allowed[a])
      return a;
  return 0;
}
struct Crop {
  bool inspect;
  int  truth;
  std::uint64_t seed, id;
};
// One worker process: greedy native streams with oracle sorting labels. Saves the
// inspection crop that decides the bin, plus 4 fps views of the current target
// (or the next belt fruit) through approach, grasp, lift and release.
void collect(const std::string& urdf, std::uint64_t first, int streams, double seconds,
             const std::string& path) {
  s::FruitStreamOptions o;
  o.articulated_physics = true;
  o.physics_backend     = s::ArticulatedBackend::Native;
  o.physics_timestep    = 1. / 960;
  o.active_capacity     = 8;
  o.watch_infeed = o.synchronized_grasp = true;
  o.visual_style                        = s::WorkcellVisualStyle::Realistic;
  o.grasp_alignment_tolerance           = .02;
  o.hold_grasp_target                   = true;
  s::FruitStreamEnvironment env(urdf, o);
  s::DevArmWristCamera      wrist(env.arm_model(), 128, 95); // the deployed camera
  std::ofstream bin(path + ".bin", std::ios::binary), csv(path + ".csv");
  auto save = [&](const s::WristInspection& in, std::uint64_t seed, const s::StreamFruit& p,
                  bool inspect) {
    if (in.crop.rgba.empty())
      return;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < in.crop.rgba.size(); i += 4)
      bin.write(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&in.crop.rgba[i]), 3);
    csv << std::format("{},{},{},{}\n", int(inspect), p.body.kind == s::FruitKind::Apple ? 0 : 1,
                       seed, p.id);
  };
  auto find = [](const s::StreamFrame& f, auto&& pred) {
    return std::find_if(f.fruit.begin(), f.fruit.end(), pred);
  };
  for (int k = 0; k < streams; ++k) {
    const std::uint64_t seed = first + k;
    env.set_perception([&](const s::StreamFrame& f, std::uint64_t id) {
      auto it = find(f, [&](const auto& p) { return p.id == id; });
      auto x  = it->body.position;
      save(wrist.inspect_actors(f.arm, env.fruit_scene(f), {x[0], x[2], x[1]}), seed, *it, true);
      return s::StreamPrediction{it->body.kind == s::FruitKind::Apple ? 0 : 1, 1.};
    });
    std::vector<s::StreamFrame> frames;
    env.record([&](const auto& f) { frames.push_back(f); }, 4);
    auto frame = env.reset(seed, .4);
    while (frame.time < seconds)
      frame = env.step(s::StreamAction(greedy(env.learning_observation()))).frame;
    env.record({});
    for (const auto& f : frames) {
      auto it = find(f, [&](const auto& p) { return p.id == f.target; });
      if (it == f.fruit.end())
        it = find(f, [](const auto& p) { return p.status == s::StreamFruitStatus::Belt; });
      if (it == f.fruit.end())
        continue;
      auto x = it->body.position;
      save(wrist.inspect_actors(f.arm, env.fruit_scene(f), {x[0], x[2], x[1]}), seed, *it, false);
    }
    std::cerr << std::format("{} stream {}/{}\n", path, k + 1, streams);
  }
}
struct Set {
  std::vector<std::uint8_t> pixels;
  std::vector<Crop>         crops;
};
void load(Set& set, const std::string& path) {
  std::ifstream csv(path + ".csv"), bin(path + ".bin", std::ios::binary);
  Crop c;
  char comma;
  int  inspect;
  std::vector<std::uint8_t> px(P);
  while (csv >> inspect >> comma >> c.truth >> comma >> c.seed >> comma >> c.id &&
         bin.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(px.data()), P)) {
    c.inspect = inspect;
    set.crops.push_back(c);
    set.pixels.insert(set.pixels.end(), px.begin(), px.end());
  }
}
// NHWC tensor of selected crops; `mirror` appends a left-right flipped copy of each.
std::pair<n::Tensor, n::Tensor> tensor(const Set& set, const std::vector<std::size_t>& rows,
                                       bool mirror) {
  std::vector<float>        x;
  std::vector<std::int64_t> y;
  for (int m = 0; m <= int(mirror); ++m)
    for (auto i : rows) {
      for (int r = 0; r < 64; ++r)
        for (int c = 0; c < 64; ++c)
          for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
            x.push_back(set.pixels[i * P + (r * 64 + (m ? 63 - c : c)) * 3 + k] / 255.f);
      y.push_back(set.crops[i].truth);
    }
  return {n::from_vector(x, {std::int64_t(y.size()), 64, 64, 3}), n::from_vector(y)};
}
// P(banana) for every crop, in batches of 512.
std::vector<double> banana(n::MobileNetClassifier& model, const Set& set) {
  std::vector<double> out;
  for (std::size_t a = 0; a < set.crops.size(); a += 512) {
    std::vector<std::size_t> rows;
    for (auto i = a; i < std::min(set.crops.size(), a + 512); ++i)
      rows.push_back(i);
    auto p = model.predict(tensor(set, rows, false).first).to_vector<float>();
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < rows.size(); ++k)
      out.push_back(p[2 * k + 1]);
  }
  return out;
}
void score(std::ostream& out, const std::string& name, n::MobileNetClassifier& model,
           const Set& set) {
  auto   p        = banana(model, set);
  int inspected = 0, inspect_ok = 0, frames = 0, frame_ok = 0, confident_wrong = 0;
  int pairs = 0, flips = 0;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < p.size(); ++i) {
    const auto& c  = set.crops[i];
    const bool  ok = (p[i] > .5) == bool(c.truth);
    if (c.inspect) {
      ++inspected;
      inspect_ok += ok;
      continue;
    }
    ++frames;
    frame_ok += ok;
    confident_wrong += !ok && std::abs(p[i] - .5) > .4;
    const Crop* b = i > 0 ? &set.crops[i - 1] : nullptr; // previous recorded frame
    if (b && !b->inspect && b->seed == c.seed && b->id == c.id) {
      ++pairs;
      flips += (p[i] > .5) != (p[i - 1] > .5);
    }
  }
  out << std::format("| {} | {}/{} ({:.1f}%) | {:.1f}% | {:.1f}% | {:.1f}% |\n", name, inspect_ok,
                     inspected, 100. * inspect_ok / inspected, 100. * frame_ok / frames,
                     100. * confident_wrong / frames, 100. * flips / pairs);
}

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  if (argc != 6)
    return 2;
  const int workers = std::stoi(argv[1]), streams = std::stoi(argv[2]);
  const double seconds = std::stod(argv[3]);
  const int    epochs  = std::stoi(argv[4]);
  const std::string out = argv[5];
  std::filesystem::create_directories(out);
  const auto assets = dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm", "../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
  const auto urdf =
      (std::filesystem::path(assets) / "Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string();
  // Separate processes keep each simulator and render cache independent.
  std::vector<pid_t> children;
  for (int w = 0; w < workers; ++w)
    if (pid_t pid = fork(); pid == 0) {
      collect(urdf, 910000 + 100 * w, streams, seconds, std::format("{}/job{:02d}", out, w));
      _exit(0);
    } else
      children.push_back(pid);
  for (auto pid : children) {
    int status = 0;
    waitpid(pid, &status, 0);
    if (!WIFEXITED(status) || WEXITSTATUS(status) != 0)
      throw std::runtime_error("collection worker failed");
  }
  const int n_train = workers * 8 / 10, n_valid = std::max(1, workers / 10);
  Set train, valid, test;
  for (int w = 0; w < workers; ++w)
    load(w < n_train ? train : w < n_train + n_valid ? valid : test,
         std::format("{}/job{:02d}", out, w));
  // Inspection crops decide the bin, so they are repeated 3x; every training crop
  // is also mirrored. Validation keeps all inspections and every 4th frame.
  std::vector<std::size_t> rows, valid_rows;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < train.crops.size(); ++i)
    for (int r = 0; r < (train.crops[i].inspect ? 3 : 1); ++r)
      rows.push_back(i);
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < valid.crops.size(); ++i)
    if (valid.crops[i].inspect || i % 4 == 0)
      valid_rows.push_back(i);
  auto [x, y]   = tensor(train, rows, true);
  auto [vx, vy] = tensor(valid, valid_rows, false);
  n::MobileNetClassifier     model(2, 64, .25, 20261105); // twice the previous width
  n::MobileClassifierOptions fit;
  fit.epochs                = epochs;
  fit.learning_rate         = .002;
  fit.batch_size            = 32;
  fit.grayscale_probability = .25;
  fit.seed                  = 20261105;
  std::ofstream log(out + "/training.csv");
  log << "epoch,training_loss,validation_loss,validation_accuracy\n";
  fit.progress = [&](const n::MobileClassifierEpoch& e) {
    log << std::format("{},{:.6f},{:.6f},{:.6f}\n", e.epoch, e.training_loss, e.validation_loss,
                       e.validation_accuracy)
        << std::flush;
  };
  auto result = model.fit(x, y, vx, vy, fit);
  model.save("figures/fruit_native_port_mobile.npz");
  std::filesystem::copy_file(out + "/training.csv", "figures/fruit_native_port_vision_training.csv",
                             std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  auto previous = n::MobileNetClassifier::load("figures/fruit_stream_physics_mobile.npz");
  std::ofstream table(out + "/test.md");
  table << std::format("Selected epoch {}. Test: {} crops from {} streams.\n\n",
                       result.selected_epoch, test.crops.size(),
                       (workers - n_train - n_valid) * streams)
        << "| Classifier | Inspection | Frames | Confident wrong | Frame flips |\n"
        << "|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n";
  score(table, "Previous (MuJoCo views, 256 px camera)", previous, test);
  score(table, "Retrained (native views, 128 px camera)", model, test);
  table.close();
  std::cout << std::ifstream(out + "/test.md").rdbuf();
}
```

Held-out test streams (24 streams, 585 inspections, 9,597 trajectory frames).
"Confident wrong" counts frames where the wrong class gets probability above 0.9;
"frame flips" counts consecutive frames of one fruit whose label changes:

| Classifier | Inspection | Frames | Confident wrong | Frame flips |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Previous (MuJoCo views, 256 px camera) | 421/585 (72.0%) | 55.6% | 22.1% | 27.4% |
| Retrained (native views, 128 px camera) | 577/585 (98.6%) | 98.7% | 0.6% | 1.5% |

Closed loop, the same greedy scheduler and corrected grasp now sort on real
camera predictions over 16 further streams of 120 s (seeds 2026120000-15, unused above):

| Classifier | Inspections correct | Correct bin | Wrong bin |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| Previous | 206/290 (71.0%) | 120 | 43 |
| Retrained | 300/304 (98.7%) | 153 | 0 |

A quarter of the old system's sorts went into the wrong bin; with the retrained
classifier none did. Most remaining frame errors are on the belt during the
approach, where the fruit is still small in the image. Mirror averaging at test
time and the narrower width-0.125 network were also tried; neither gave a clear
gain over this model. The [training log|file:figures/fruit_native_port_vision_training.csv]
records each epoch.

## Native video: greedy scheduler with the corrected grasp

The final run combines the greedy rule with the corrected grasp skill for 60
seconds at 0.4 fruit/s, with the retrained MobileNet classifying each
wrist-camera crop. The camera inset shows the current class and probability
beside the foreground box; labels are drawn after inference and do not enter
the model or controller.

```{cpp, results="markdown", nix-shell="git+file:../../..#cpp", cmd="export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=$(printenv DATAMUNGE_CAD_PKG_CONFIG_PATH || printenv PKG_CONFIG_PATH); c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && DATAMUNGE_LINKED_CORE=$(pkg-config --variable=prefix datamunge) OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 {bin}"}
#include <algorithm>
#include <chrono>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
namespace s = dm::sim;
namespace c = dm::cad;
namespace n = dm::nn;
void append(c::Scene& scene, c::Scene extra) {
  int base = int(scene.meshes.size()), tex = int(scene.textures.size());
  for (auto& m : extra.meshes)
    scene.meshes.push_back(std::move(m));
  for (auto& t : extra.textures)
    scene.textures.push_back(std::move(t));
  for (auto o : extra.objects) {
    o.mesh_index += base;
    o.parent = -1;
    for (int* p :
         {&o.texture_index, &o.normal_map_index, &o.roughness_map_index, &o.metallic_map_index})
      if (*p >= 0)
        *p += tex;
    scene.AddObject(o);
  }
}
// Greedy rule: intercept whenever any option is feasible, preferring the leader late.
std::size_t greedy(const dm::rl::DiscreteObservation& x) {
  for (std::size_t a : {2, 1, 4, 3})
    if (x.allowed[a])
      return a;
  return 0;
}
n::Tensor rgb(const c::RenderResult& image) {
  std::vector<float> v;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < image.rgba.size(); i += 4)
    for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k)
      v.push_back(image.rgba[i + k] / 255.f);
  return n::from_vector(v, {1, image.height, image.width, 3});
}
// Display-only annotation: call after inference on the clean crop. The label
// follows the current box and is kept inside the camera image at every edge.
void wrist_overlay(
    c::RenderResult&   image,
    const s::ImageBox& box,
    int                prediction,
    double             probability) {
  const int  scale = image.width >= 192 ? 2 : 1, padding = 2;
  const bool detected = box.width > 0 && box.height > 0;
  if (detected)
    for (int y = std::max(0, box.y); y < std::min(image.height, box.y + box.height); ++y)
      for (int x = std::max(0, box.x); x < std::min(image.width, box.x + box.width); ++x) {
        if (x >= box.x + 2 && y >= box.y + 2 && x < box.x + box.width - 2 &&
            y < box.y + box.height - 2)
          continue;
        const auto i      = 4 * (y * image.width + x);
        image.rgba[i]     = 30;
        image.rgba[i + 1] = 245;
        image.rgba[i + 2] = 120;
      }
  const auto label =
      !detected ? std::string("NO DETECTION")
      : prediction < 0
          ? std::string("UNKNOWN")
          : std::format("{} P {:.3f}", prediction == 0 ? "APPLE" : "BANANA", probability);
  const int width = int(label.size()) * 6 * scale + 2 * padding, height = 7 * scale + 2 * padding;
  const int x           = std::clamp(detected ? box.x : 2, 0, std::max(0, image.width - width));
  const int preferred_y = !detected ? 2 : box.y >= height ? box.y - height : box.y + box.height;
  const int y           = std::clamp(preferred_y, 0, std::max(0, image.height - height));
  for (int yy = y; yy < std::min(image.height, y + height); ++yy)
    for (int xx = x; xx < std::min(image.width, x + width); ++xx) {
      const auto i = 4 * (yy * image.width + xx);
      for (int ch = 0; ch < 3; ++ch)
        image.rgba[i + ch] = static_cast<unsigned char>(.15 * image.rgba[i + ch] + .85 * 12);
      image.rgba[i + 3] = 255;
    }
  c::draw_text(image, label, x + padding, y + padding, scale, {.12f, .96f, .47f, 1});
}

int main() {
  try {
    const std::string out = "build/fruit_native_port/";
    std::filesystem::create_directories(out);
    const auto assets = dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm", "../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
    const auto urdf =
        (std::filesystem::path(assets) / "Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf")
            .string();
    s::FruitStreamOptions options;
    options.articulated_physics = true;
    options.physics_backend     = s::ArticulatedBackend::Native;
    options.physics_timestep    = 1. / 960;
    options.active_capacity     = 8;
    options.watch_infeed        = true;
    options.synchronized_grasp  = true;
    options.visual_style        = s::WorkcellVisualStyle::Realistic;
    options.grasp_alignment_tolerance = .02; // close within 20 mm of the moving fruit
    options.hold_grasp_target         = true; // stop re-aiming once a finger touches
    s::FruitStreamEnvironment env(urdf, options);
    s::DevArmWristCamera      wrist(env.arm_model(), 128, 95);
    wrist.set_render_threads(8);
    auto classifier = n::MobileNetClassifier::load("figures/fruit_native_port_mobile.npz");
    std::ofstream perception(out + "perception.csv");
    perception << "time,id,label,confidence,x,y,width,height\n";
    env.set_perception([&](const s::StreamFrame& f, std::uint64_t id) {
      auto it =
          std::find_if(f.fruit.begin(), f.fruit.end(), [&](const auto& p) { return p.id == id; });
      if (it == f.fruit.end())
        throw std::runtime_error("missing tracked fruit");
      auto p     = it->body.position;
      auto image = wrist.inspect_actors(f.arm, env.fruit_scene(f), {p[0], p[2], p[1]});
      s::StreamPrediction result;
      if (!image.crop.rgba.empty()) {
        auto prob         = classifier.predict(rgb(image.crop)).to_vector<float>();
        result.label      = prob[1] > prob[0];
        result.confidence = prob[result.label];
      }
      perception << f.time << ',' << id << ',' << result.label << ',' << result.confidence << ','
                 << image.box.x << ',' << image.box.y << ',' << image.box.width << ','
                 << image.box.height << '\n';
      return result;
    });
    const int                   fps = 15, seconds = 60;
    std::vector<s::StreamFrame> frames;
    env.record(
        [&](const auto& f) {
          if (f.time <= seconds + 1e-8)
            frames.push_back(f);
        },
        fps);
    auto begin = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
    auto frame = env.reset(2026113001, .4);
    while (frame.time < seconds) {
      frame = env.step(s::StreamAction(greedy(env.learning_observation()))).frame;
    }
    env.record({});
    double sim_time =
        std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - begin).count();
    std::ofstream trace(out + "trajectory.csv");
    trace << "time,arrivals,correct,wrong,missed,penetration,effort,joint_speed,finger_speed\n";
    for (auto& f : frames) {
      if (f.physics_backend != s::ArticulatedBackend::Native || !f.articulated_physics ||
          !f.arm.measured_joints || f.training_proxy || f.synthetic_perception)
        throw std::runtime_error("incorrect native frame provenance");
      trace << f.time << ',' << f.counts.arrivals << ',' << f.counts.correct << ','
            << f.counts.wrong << ',' << f.counts.missed << ',' << f.maximum_penetration << ','
            << f.maximum_effort_fraction << ',' << f.maximum_joint_speed << ','
            << f.maximum_finger_speed << '\n';
    }
    if (frames.size() != fps * seconds + 1)
      throw std::runtime_error("native trajectory incomplete");
    auto      scenery = s::workcell_presentation(env.arm_model().static_scene(), true);
    c::Camera camera;
    camera.position     = {-1.65, -2.25, 1.65};
    camera.target       = {-.05, 0, .6};
    camera.vertical_fov = 40;
    auto quality        = s::workcell_presentation_options(960, 640);
    quality.threads     = 8;
    std::unique_ptr<c::CudaRenderer> gpu;
    if (dm::compute::probe({dm::compute::Backend::CUDA, 0}).available)
      gpu = std::make_unique<c::CudaRenderer>();
    c::VideoWriter video(out + "native_port.mp4", 960, 640, fps);
    begin                    = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
    bool saved_labelled_view = false;
    for (std::size_t k = 0; k < fps * seconds; ++k) {
      auto& f     = frames[k];
      auto  fixed = scenery;
      append(fixed, s::workcell_presentation(env.arm_model().robot_scene(f.arm)));
      append(fixed, wrist.housing(f.arm));
      c::PreparedScene prepared(std::move(fixed));
      auto             actors = env.fruit_scene(f);
      auto image = gpu ? gpu->render(prepared, s::workcell_presentation(actors), camera, quality)
                       : prepared.render(s::workcell_presentation(actors), camera, quality);
      c::RenderResult inset;
      auto            focus = std::find_if(
          f.fruit.begin(), f.fruit.end(), [&](const auto& p) { return p.id == f.target; });
      if (focus == f.fruit.end())
        focus = std::find_if(f.fruit.begin(), f.fruit.end(), [](const auto& p) {
          return p.status == s::StreamFruitStatus::Belt;
        });
      int    display_prediction  = -1;
      double display_probability = 0;
      if (focus == f.fruit.end()) {
        inset = wrist.capture_actors(f.arm, actors);
        wrist_overlay(inset, {}, -1, 0);
      } else {
        auto p    = focus->body.position;
        auto view = wrist.inspect_actors(f.arm, actors, {p[0], p[2], p[1]});
        // Infer before annotating: the model never sees the box or text.
        if (!view.crop.rgba.empty()) {
          const auto probabilities = classifier.predict(rgb(view.crop)).to_vector<float>();
          display_prediction       = probabilities[1] > probabilities[0] ? 1 : 0;
          display_probability      = probabilities[display_prediction];
        }
        wrist_overlay(view.rgb, view.box, display_prediction, display_probability);
        inset = std::move(view.rgb);
      }
      // Enlarge the 128-pixel sensor view 2x so its box label remains readable.
      for (int y = 0; y < 256; ++y)
        for (int x = 0; x < 256; ++x)
          for (int j = 0; j < 4; ++j)
            image.rgba[4 * ((20 + y) * 960 + 20 + x) + j] =
                inset.rgba[4 * ((y / 2) * 128 + x / 2) + j];
      c::draw_text(image, "NATIVE VSIM - GREEDY SCHEDULER, ALIGNED GRASP", 20, 570, 2);
      c::draw_text(
          image,
          "T " + std::to_string(f.time).substr(0, 4) + "  ARRIVED " +
              std::to_string(f.counts.arrivals) + "  SORTED " + std::to_string(f.counts.correct) +
              "  MISSED " + std::to_string(f.counts.missed),
          20,
          600,
          2);
      video.append(image);
      if (!saved_labelled_view && display_prediction >= 0) {
        image.save(out + "camera_prediction.png");
        saved_labelled_view = true;
      }
      if (k == fps * seconds - 1)
        image.save(out + "poster.png");
      if (k % 60 == 0)
        std::cerr << "Native render " << k << "/" << fps * seconds << '\n';
    }
    video.finish();
    std::ofstream metrics(out + "metrics.json");
    metrics << "{\"engine\":\"" << s::articulated_physics_version(options.physics_backend)
            << "\",\"scheduler\":\"greedy rule (native DQN did not beat it on validation)\""
            << ",\"grasp_alignment_tolerance\":" << options.grasp_alignment_tolerance
            << ",\"hold_grasp_target\":" << (options.hold_grasp_target ? "true" : "false")
            << ",\"seed\":2026113001,\"sim_seconds\":" << seconds
            << ",\"arrival_rate\":0.4,\"frames\":" << frames.size()
            << ",\"simulation_wall_seconds\":" << sim_time << ",\"render_wall_seconds\":"
            << std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - begin).count()
            << ",\"maximum_penetration\":" << frames.back().maximum_penetration
            << ",\"maximum_effort_fraction\":" << frames.back().maximum_effort_fraction
            << ",\"arrivals\":" << frames.back().counts.arrivals
            << ",\"correct\":" << frames.back().counts.correct
            << ",\"wrong\":" << frames.back().counts.wrong
            << ",\"missed\":" << frames.back().counts.missed << "}\n";
    metrics.close();
    std::filesystem::copy_file(
        out + "native_port.mp4",
        "figures/fruit_native_port.mp4",
        std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
    std::filesystem::copy_file(
        out + "poster.png",
        "figures/fruit_native_port.png",
        std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
    std::filesystem::copy_file(
        out + "metrics.json",
        "figures/fruit_native_port.json",
        std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
    const auto& n = frames.back().counts;
    std::cout << std::format("Native vsim, 960 Hz, {} s: {} arrivals, {} correct, {} wrong, {} "
                             "missed.\n\n\\video(figures/fruit_native_port.mp4)\n",
                             seconds, n.arrivals, n.correct, n.wrong, n.missed);
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
    return 1;
  }
}

```

// result_begin: markdown
Native vsim, 960 Hz, 60 s: 19 arrivals, 6 correct, 1 wrong, 11 missed.

\video(figures/fruit_native_port.mp4)
// result_end

The corrected grasp is the change that matters. With the same greedy scheduler,
it raises correct sorts on the eight test streams from 49 to 68 (+39%) and stable
grasps from 55 to 75, while attempts barely change. Both learned schedulers
gain less from it: the MuJoCo-trained DQN rises only from 42 to 50, and the
natively trained DQN reaches 40 because it attempts far fewer fruit (71 vs 118).
Arrivals exceed arm capacity about threefold, so most fruit are still missed by
every scheduler. Further gains must come from a faster pick cycle or a better
grasp skill, not from scheduling.

The 60-second native run above (seed 2026113001) has 19 arrivals: 6 correct
sorts, 1 wrong bin and 11 misses, with the rest still on the belt. The old
20-second transfer clip had zero sorts. The wrong bin is most likely a perception error
(MobileNet on rendered wrist RGB), which the comparison table removes by using
synthetic labels. Maximum contact penetration is 1.6 mm; peak actuator effort
fraction is 1.0. The [measured run record|file:figures/fruit_native_port.json]
retains the options, seed, timings and backend provenance. Separate analytic
tests verify actual contact-driven lifting.
